In article <NF2SBGS1@cc.swarthmore.edu>, rbrooks1@cc.swarthmore.edu (Rob Brooks) writes:
> Ok, this is going to sound kind of silly but I'm a little confused about
> something.  In a lot of the postings on this group people give the commands
> in nethack with a # immediately before the command (i.e. #apply or #offer).
>  What does this signify?  Is it something I need to know to help me with
> the game?

Yes.  Most commands are entered directly, like i="inventory" or p="pay."
A small set of commands don't fit on the keyboard (so I assume) and
so are entered after hitting the # key.  They are called extended
commands, and you can get help on them by selecting "?" and then option
"h."

I would say they're not _vital_ to the game; you might win without using
any of them.  But they include some of the most useful non-fighting
actions.  They mostly make the game more fun and flexible.

